
h1 Drives, folders, and documents API

h2 Example: create a drive
curl -X POST "$POLYGRES_BASE_URL/v1/workspaces/$WORKSPACE_ID/drives" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $POLYGRES_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Idempotency-Key: create-handbooks-1" \
  -d '{"name":"Handbooks"}'

h2 Resource responses
{
  "id": "DRIVE_UUID",
  "name": "Handbooks",
  "version": "1",
  "status": "provisioning",
  "document_count": 0,
  "indexed_document_count": 0,
  "index_snapshot_id": null
}
{
  "id": "FOLDER_UUID",
  "name": "Policies",
  "parent_folder_id": null,
  "version": "1"
}

h2 Add and replace text
curl -X POST "$POLYGRES_BASE_URL/v1/drives/$DRIVE_ID/documents" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $POLYGRES_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Idempotency-Key: handbook-text-v1" \
  -d '{"documents":[{"external_id":"handbook","text":"Refunds are available within 30 days.","metadata":{"edition":1}}]}'
curl -X PUT "$POLYGRES_BASE_URL/v1/drives/$DRIVE_ID/documents/$DOCUMENT_ID" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $POLYGRES_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Idempotency-Key: handbook-text-v2" \
  -d '{"text":"Refunds are available within 45 days.","metadata":{"edition":2},"folder_id":null}'

h2 Progressive text imports
curl -X POST "$POLYGRES_BASE_URL/v1/drives/$DRIVE_ID/documents" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $POLYGRES_API_KEY" \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Idempotency-Key: library-text-group-0001" \
  -H "X-Ingestion-Mode: progressive" \
  --data-binary @documents.json

h2 GET /v1/workspaces/{workspace_id}/drives
Name | Location | Value | Required
workspace_id | path | string | Yes
limit | query | integer | Optional
cursor | query | string | Optional
Field | Type | Present | Constraints
data | array of object | Yes | 
data[].id | string | Yes | uuid
data[].name | string | Yes | 
data[].version | string | Yes | 
data[].etag | string | Yes | 
next_cursor | string or null | Yes | 

